# Create real directories and per-file symlinks instead of folding whole
# directories into one link. Folding would make ~/.config itself a link into
# this repo on a fresh machine, so every app writing ~/.config/<anything>
# would write into the repo. Per-file links keep repo contents explicit.
--no-folding

# Packages name hidden targets with a dot- prefix, dot-config linking to
# ~/.config, so repo content stays visible to rg/fd/nvim. Default the flag
# here so a manual stow run can never link literal dot-star names.
# NOTE: stow parses this file loosely; punctuation in comments can break it.
--dotfiles
